        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "0.6 acre site at Rashane, Ardrahan** with castle views.\r\n\r\nA fantastic opportunity to secure a wellproportioned 0.6 acre site in the peaceful townland of Rashane, just minutes from Ardrahan village. This scenic plot enjoys uninterrupted views of Ardrahan Castle, offering a truly unique and charming backdrop for a future home. The site sits within a quiet rural setting surrounded by open countryside, yet remains close to everyday amenities including Ardrahan National School, GAA facilities, train station, shops and cafés. It’s an ideal balance of tranquillity and convenience. \r\n\r\nCommuters will appreciate the excellent connectivity, with quick access to the M18 linking directly to Galway, Gort, Ennis, Shannon and Limerick. Whether travelling daily or occasionally, this location provides effortless movement while still offering the calm of countryside living. This is a Local Need Planning Area, making it a strong option for applicants with ties to the Ardrahan community. It’s perfectly suited to those wishing to remain close to family roots, return home, or build a longterm residence within a supportive rural setting. \r\n\r\nKey Features: \r\n- Approx. 0.6 acre site \r\n- Stunning castle views \r\n- Peaceful rural location \r\n- Minutes from Ardrahan village & train station \r\n- Excellent M18 access for Galway, Gort, Ennis, Shannon & Limerick \r\n- Local Need Planning Area \r\n- Ideal for a oneoff dwelling (subject to planning permission) \r\n\r\nA rare chance to build in a scenic, historic and highly convenient location."
